rks affect crew cooperation and professional communication. Weak memory for numbers could affect attention.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology. Weaknesses: difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education. So decision quality, stress resilience good, technical competence good, but communication and teamwork issues, and lack of development.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Weaknesses: regarded as a know-it-all, has a hot temper. So reliability, problem solving, responsibility good, but hot temper and know-it-all may affect crew cooperation.\n\nWe need best overall fit. Which candidate balances? B has strong reliability and stress, but nasty remarks is serious for crew cooperation. D has strong problem solving and responsibility, but hot temper is concerning for stress resilience and crew cooperation. C has good decision and calm, but communication issues and egocentric. A has leadership but show-off and not open to new ideas.\n\nProbably D might be best if hot temper can be mitigated? But hot temper is serious for long-distance flights. B's nasty remarks also serious. C's communication issues also serious. A's show-off may affect crew but maybe less severe? Not open to new ideas also problematic.\n\nWe need to pick one. I think D's strengths are many: concentration, problem solving, responsibility, adaptability to unexpected events. The hot temper is a concern but maybe less than egocentric or nasty remarks? Hot temper could affect calmness under pressure. But D responds adequately to unexpected events, indicating some calmness. Might be okay.\n\nThus I will recommend Candidate D, but note concerns.\n\nWe must produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote D.\n\nLet's craft."}
